## 3. END-TO-END OPERATIONAL WORKFLOWS

### Workflow A: Inbound Raw Material Receiving & Inspection (`SOP-REC-001` / `Form-REC-001`)
1. **Dock Arrival & 30-Minute SLA Timer:** When a supplier delivery arrives at the Low Care (Black Zone) dock, the system starts a **30-minute logging SLA countdown** (`> 1 hour unlogged = automatic Shipment Quarantine warning`).
2. **PO/DR & Invoice Matching:** Jade Q. Dela Cruz selects or enters the Report No. (e.g., `RR-2026-00001`), PO/DR Number (e.g., `PO-2026-1001`), Supplier Name (e.g., `P.L. Sebastian Corporation`, `Lucky Roma Trading`, `JCT Wheat & Sugar Products`, `Davao Great Wall Trading, Inc.`, `Golden Fortune Trading Incorporated`, `Local Poultry Coop`, `Mandaue Libertad Flexible Packaging Inc.`, `C-One`), Carrier/Plate #, and Invoice Type (`Sales Invoice`, `Charge Invoice`, `Delivery Receipt`) + Invoice #.
3. **Mandatory Quality & Food-Safety Receiving Gates (Hard Validation Checklists):**
   * **Gate 1 — Delivery Vehicle & Packaging Integrity:** Check for punctures, moisture stains, pest infestation, or dented/rusted cans. Outer cartons must be stripped before staging into Dry Room 2.
   * **Gate 2 — Expiration Date & Minimum Shelf-Life Check:** System blocks receipt into active stock if `Expiration Date <= Current Date` (or `< 30 days` without QA override). Suspect/expired items are flagged for immediate rejection at the delivery truck (24-hour supplier return rule) or routed directly to the Exterior Quarantine Cabinet.
   * **Gate 3 — Commodity-Specific Checks:**
     * *Cold Room (`RM-FAT-001` Magnolia Buttercup):* Mandatory check that delivery temperature is `≤ 0°C` AND **individual butter block cellophanes carry indelible supplier expiration date stickers** (`0°C / Cellophane Sticker Checked`). Blocks without stickers must be rejected.
     * *Egg Room / Wet Room (`RM-DRY-001` Fresh Eggs):* Inspect for micro-cracks and enforce mandatory **Egg Sanitization Rinse Protocol** (`Rinsed / Pass`, verified by Vincent S. Plaza / Jade Q. Dela Cruz) prior to Wet Room entry.
     * *Fortification & Food-Grade Certificates (`CoA / CoC`):* Verify status (`Verified on File`, `Pending Follow-up`, `Missing - Hold`). Specifically check RA 8172 potassium iodate compliance for salt (`RM-SWT-003`), RA 8976 Vitamin A/Iron fortification for flour, and US FDA 21 CFR 177.1520(c)3.2a / Mandaue Libertad CoA (`J.O. No. JB-4780`) & CoC (`MLCP-QA-0035`) for Biscocho wrappers.
4. **Dual-UoM Quantity & Financial Discrepancy Calculation (`JJB-WAREHOUSE RECEIVING REPORT` logic):**
   * User enters `Qty Ordered` (Primary UoM), `Qty Received` (Good Primary UoM), `Qty Undelivered / Return / Damaged`, and `Unit Price (₱)`.
   * System automatically calculates:
     $$\text{Total Net Qty Received} = \text{Qty Received (Primary)} \times \text{Conversion Factor}$$
     $$\text{Qty Undelivered/Damaged} = \text{Qty Ordered} - \text{Qty Received}$$
     $$\text{Undelivered/Return Amount (₱)} = \text{Qty Undelivered/Damaged} \times \text{Unit Price}$$
     $$\text{Total Received Value to be PAID (₱)} = \text{Qty Received} \times \text{Unit Price}$$
     $$\text{VAT (12.0\%)} \text{ and Grand Total Valuation Summary}$$
   * If `Qty Damaged > 0` or `Overall Shipment Status == "Damaged"`, highlight row in **Amber/Red** to alert Accounts Payable (Jeanifer S. Sauping).

### Workflow B: Put-Away, Storage Location & FEFO Lot Management (`SOP-WAR-001` / `Form-WAR-001`)
1. **Room & Bin Assignment:** Accepted lots are assigned to their designated `Storage Room` (`Dry Room 1`, `Dry Room 2`, `Cold Room`, `Wet Room`, `Egg Room`, `Milk Room`) and specific `Location / Bin #` (e.g., `HDPE-BIN-01`, `PALLET-DR1-A2`, `FREEZER-CR-01`).
2. **Perpetual Balance & FEFO Queueing:**
   * Each received lot is tracked individually by `Supplier Lot/Batch #` and `Expiration Date`.
   * System sorts available lots per SKU strictly by **First-Expired, First-Out (FEFO)**—oldest expiration date at the top of the pick queue with color-coded expiry badges:
     * **EXPIRED (`<= 0 days`):** Red badge — Auto-locked from issuance; prompt immediate transfer to Exterior Quarantine Cabinet (`Form-NCR-001`).
     * **CRITICAL FEFO (`1 to 30 days`):** Orange badge — Priority issuance alert (e.g., `RM-DRY-001` Fresh Eggs expiring `2026-11-15`).
     * **WARNING (`31 to 60 days`):** Yellow badge.
     * **HEALTHY (`> 60 days` or `N/A` for non-perishable packaging):** Green badge.
3. **Stock Health Status Engine:**
   * Compare `Current Net Balance` (and `Equivalent Bulk Packs = Current Net Balance / Conversion Factor`) against `Reorder Threshold`:
     * `Current Net Balance <= 0`: **OUT OF STOCK / CRITICAL DEPLETION**
     * `Current Net Balance <= Reorder Threshold`: **REORDER NEEDED**
     * `Current Net Balance <= Reorder Threshold * 1.25`: **LOW STOCK**
     * Otherwise: **HEALTHY**

